<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hemavathi</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Henjeru</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hemavathi is a village in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andhra-pradesh">Andhra Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, near the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a>, known in medieval inscriptions as Henjeru. It was the main capital of the Nolamba dynasty in the 9th and 10th centuries. Its temples, above all the Doddeshvara temple, preserve finely carved black-stone pillars and ceilings of Nolamba art, and some of its sculptures were removed to museums.</p></div>
